The quantitative example now becomes useful. The speaker says that one property can gross about $\$3{,}000\text{--}\$5{,}500$ per month. Let us annualize that carefully: $\begin{aligned}
G_{\mathrm{property},y}
&= 12\,G_{\mathrm{property},m} \\
&\approx 12 \times (\$3{,}000\text{--}\$5{,}500) \\
&\approx \$36{,}000\text{--}\$66{,}000.\end{aligned}$

