p.src:
A simple bookkeeping identity expresses the logic: $R_{\mathrm{trip}}
=
R_{\mathrm{lodging}}
+
R_{\mathrm{transport}}
+
R_{\mathrm{premium}}.$ This is not the speaker’s notation, but it is the cleanest way to preserve his point. The same traveler can support multiple streams of gross revenue.

